Answer: In the early stages of the COVID-19 pandemic in early 2020, the CDC did not recommend that healthy members of the general public wear face masks. According to the provided text, the CDC's official position at the time was that "CDC does not recommend that people who are well wear a face mask to protect themselves from respiratory illnesses, including Covid-19," with authorities "previously only recommended masks for those who are sick and people, such as health care workers, who frequently interact with the sick."

